### =====================================================================
### Topic 7 Course Registration API (port 8087). VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### =====================================================================

### All courses (loaded by StartupDataLoader)
GET http://localhost:8087/courses

### One course
GET http://localhost:8087/courses/1

### Derived query: findByTitleContainingIgnoreCase
GET http://localhost:8087/courses/search?title=java

### Create a valid course -> 201 (no capacity given, so school.default-course-capacity is used)
POST http://localhost:8087/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "MTH201", "title": "Further Maths", "teacher": "Mr. Musa" }

### Create an INVALID course -> 400 with field messages
POST http://localhost:8087/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "", "title": "", "capacity": 500 }

### Duplicate code -> 409
POST http://localhost:8087/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "CS101", "title": "Copy of Java" }

### Enroll in Robotics Club (capacity 2). Send it 3 times: the 3rd gives 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8087/courses/3/enroll

### Course that does not exist -> 404
GET http://localhost:8087/courses/999

### Delete -> 204
DELETE http://localhost:8087/courses/2

### --- Actuator (the health dashboard) ---
GET http://localhost:8087/actuator/health

###
GET http://localhost:8087/actuator/info

### The auto-configuration report: what Boot set up, and why
GET http://localhost:8087/actuator/conditions
